      "height": 50,
      "id": "mup2hnx8z5293o",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "A short tour of Design Studio, using this sample prototype. Open things as you go and change what you like. Everything here is yours to edit or delete.",
      "seed": 1484527850,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "A short tour of Design Studio, using this sample prototype. Open things as you go and change what you\nlike. Everything here is yours to edit or delete.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1384717537,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 1000,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 80
    },
    {
      "autoResize": false,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "height": 40,
      "id": "mup2hnx9b357wc",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "When you are done, delete this prototype from its … menu, or ask your agent to. Then start your own with New prototype on the Prototypes page.",
      "seed": 372125788,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "When you are done, delete this prototype from its … menu, or ask your agent to. Then start your own with New prototype on the\nPrototypes page.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 735725543,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 1000,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 150
    },
    {
      "autoResize": false,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "frameId": "mup2hooae4hn3k",
      "height": 225,
      "id": "mup2ho6enx5c3u",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "originalText": "The navigation shows the prototype's folder as it is on disk. Choose Reveal in Finder in the … menu to see for yourself.\n\nA view is a screen (.tsx). A document is a page of writing (.md). A canvas is a page to arrange things on (.excalidraw), like this one. A folder only organizes.\n\nThe star means the prototype opens on that file. Right-click another and choose Set as start.",
      "seed": 1100213860,
      "text": "The navigation shows the prototype's folder as it is on\ndisk. Choose Reveal in Finder in the … menu to see for\nyourself.\n\nA view is a screen (.tsx). A document is a page of\nwriting (.md). A canvas is a page to arrange things on\n(.excalidraw), like this one. A folder only organizes.\n\nThe star means the prototype opens on that file.\nRight-click another and choose Set as start.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1941795286,
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "width": 460,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 320
    },
